        <mxCell id="noteDirection" value="Dependencies only ever point downwards

No model imports a controller, and no controller contains SQL — which is what keeps a rule in one place rather than repeated once per route." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="760" y="470" width="340" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteClass" value="Why not a class diagram

The models are collections of functions over SQL. Drawing them as UML classes with associations and inheritance would show relationships the code does not have — which an examiner reading the source would notice." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#eef2ff;strokeColor=#4f46e5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4338ca;" vertex="1" parent="1">
